R. D. Davis <rdd@access1.digex.net> wrote:

>I've tried inserting the RQDX3 into both the AB and CD parts of slot
>No. 4, but it still doesn't seem to be working.  The system does pass
>all of its self-tests, and I get to:

[...]
>  ?4C DEVINACT, DUA0
>  ?06 HLT INST
>      PC = 00000EE6
>  Failure.
[...]

It turned out that the above was due to a grant continuity problem.  I
was mistakenly thinking that slot 3 in a BA23 could only be used for
memory, hence, I didn't realize that without something stuck in slot 3
for grant continuity, that things wouldn't work.

After following the instructions from the VMS FAQ for breaking into a
VAX, I've now got a VAX running MicroVMS V4.6.  :-) I'm not sure just
how complete the OS is, but hopefully there's enough there to play
with Macro-32.

One further note: the following jumper settings are correct:

>Should the RQDX3 be in a different slot?  Do I need to change any of
>the jumper settings?  Here's how the jumpers are set on this RQDX3:

>     ------------------------------------------------------------------- 
>    |                                o  o 
>    |                                o  o  B1 to B4
>    |                                o  o
>    |                                o  o 
>    |                                         o  o   o  o
>    |     o--o                                  C1 & C2       o--o  o  o
>    |     o  o                                                  D1 & D2  
>    |     o--o   A1 to A11                
>    |     o  o
>    |     o  o 
>    |     o  o 
>    |     o--o          Note: I don't see any numbering on the jumpers 
>    |     o--o                on this board, so I made up my own jumper
>    |     o  o                numbering system.
