A real DEC H9642 won't have any problems.  Variants of the this cabinet
held 3 RA80/81/82's, each of which is about 150 pounds.  You're
nowhere near this limit.

There were different variations of the 9642, though, and some seem
beefier than others.  Certainly the ones that had RA80's in them
seemed a bit stiffer than the ones that I often see 11/23 and RL02
systems in.  

The only problem with putting heavy things on the top of racks, in
my experience, is the back stress with lifting them up to that
height.  After all, you're back is more valuable than the stuff in the
rack!

