This past Friday, DEC had another "adjustment". There was an individual of
many  years that was no longer needed by DEC. 

His heart attack was Saturday. His death with Monday. His name was Bill
Rebeau (pronownced RA-BOW). Bill served a proud career in the US Air Force
before his move to DEC and served many devoted years at DEC.

Maybe DEC could have done a better job of "letting him down"...who
knows...not my job and I'm sure not the job of a lot of others. 

What I remember is that there was a company I worked for that stumbled all
of a sudden. Great technology and, at one time, mostly really great folks.
Many folks tried to hang on like Bill in the hopes that things might turn
around. Maybe for Bill that was the case and the shock of other's failures
was too much for even Bill to adjust to.

Bill's legacy is honesty and integrity.

May he rest in peace....



