Tom Champlin wrote:
> 
> I am attempting to buy more memory for a Dec 33MHz / 486 machine and
> need to understand if the machine has parity or non-parity, whatever
> that means.  Does anybody know?? The memory vendors couldn't help
> 
It depends on the model of machine - most of the DECpc line required
parity SIMMS. (The XL and XL server can use either). Also, the LPx and
LPv etc have problems with some 8MB SIMMS - you may want to use 4 4MB's
instead). Celebris, Venturis, and Starion use non-parity.

Greg



