>is very little room... but I always thought about making some room for
>something like an RD32 and using an RQDX3...

In storage I have a VT180 - a VT100 with a 4 slot backplane - that
has a KDJ11-B (11/23 + boot ROM's + two serial ports), a 256 kbyte
memory board, and a Andromeda disk controller that makes a
single 3.5" HH MFM hard drive look like 3 non-removable RL02's.
All it really needs now is some form of removable storage.
I'd add a RQDX3 and a 5.25" RX33 compatible floppy, or a TU58, but
I'm afraid of overloading the already maxed out VT180 power supply.
(the +12V supply in mine can barely spin up the MFM hard drive.)

