In article <51v3u5$nhb@thighmaster.admin.lsa.umich.edu>, khillig@Be.Chem.LSA.UMich.Edu (Kurt Hillig) writes:

:We're trying to get IDL running on a VAXstation running VMS 6.2 and
:DECwindows/Motif 1.1 (just installed earlier this week); but IDL keeps
:complaining about an ident mismatch with the shared image
:SYS$LIBRARY:DECW$XLIBSHARE.EXE.... 

   Take a look at the version requirements for IDL, and see if there
   isn't a requirement for a more recent version of DECwindows.  (The
   V1.1 release is pretty old -- V1.2-4 is the current release.)

   The only similar image I can find is DECW$XLIBSHR, hence I'd assume
   that this DECW$XLIBSHARE file is very old, or that there is a (possibly
   invalid) logical name around that is redirecting the reference to this
   (outdated) file.

:On inspection, this file is dated from 1992, while the rest of the OS
:files are dated 1995; so we suspect it's a leftover from an earlier
:version of the system.

   What's somewhat more interesting than file dates is the file's
   imbedded version indentification.

:But, we haven't been able to figure out where to find this file for
:VMS 6.2 - I assume that it's somewhere on the VMS CD, or on the DW/Motif
:CD, or one of the 11 condist CD's, but all of our guesses as to just where
:to look have been fruitless (and we've installed a lot of useless junk in
:the process). 

  First, see what version of DECwindows or DECwindows Motif is required
  by IDL, (and license, acquire,) and install that version.  Then check to
  see what the GSMATCH values are for the particular image that is blowing
  up -- see the DCL command ANALYZE/IMAGE/OUTPUT=file.exe, and then search
  or edit the file for the image(s) in question.  Compare these values with
  the values of the images you have...

  The other obvious approach involves contacting whomever supports IDL and
  asking them for assistance.

:Can anyone tell us where this file comes from (i.e. what to tell VMSINSTAL to
:install)?  Please respond by e-mail, unles you really think thousands of other
:people are dying for the answer.... 

