I believe every UNIX vendor out their uses Tuxedo for their TPC-C
numbers.  Only the NT boxes have gone the non-Tuxedo route (although
HP's NT number uses Tuxedo).  Basically Tuxedo buys
you a lot in very large configurations.  Vendors who don't use
it are most likely throwing performance away.  We don't use
Tuxedo because of a lack of kernel threads, we use it for other
reasons.
  
