In article <324658D3.1098@royalmail.co.uk>, Robin Birch <birchr@royalmail.co.uk> writes:

:I have aquired the guts of a uVAX II which I am installing in a BA23
:at home.  I assume that the processor and memory, I have an 8MByte
:board, go in two of the top board slots, the ones that have the CD
:slots.

   The CD interconnect is present in the top *3* (three) slots of
   the BA23.

:If this is so, which one goes in slot 1, the processor or the memory?.

   BA23:
	The CPU traditionally sits in the first slot, with one or two
	memory modules directly adjacent.  With one memory board, the
	Q22 portion of the third Q-bus slot can be occupied by a dual
	Q-bus controller (the Ethernet controller is a common choice)
	or by a Q-bus grant continuity card.  The serpentine Q22 slot
	pattern commences in slot 4 in the BA23.  
   BA123:
	The first four slots of the BA123 are Q22/CD, with the Q22
	serpentine pattern commencing in slot 5.
   BA2xx/BA4xx:
	All (Q-bus) slots are Q22/CD slots in the BA2xx and BA4xx
	Q-bus enclosures.  Some of the specific enclosures in these
	two enclosure series have dedicated slots for the processor
	and memory -- these slots are not Q-bus nor Q22/CD slots.
   VAXstation 3520/3540 (BA??):
	The Q-bus is present only if the M-bus to Q-bus adapter (the
	DWFQA) is configured.  Only a limited number of (specified)
	Q-bus widgets are supported.

