In article <Pine.OSF.3.94.960923173725.9519A-100000@grace.isc.rit.edu>, Brett Lavin <bwl9099@osfmail.isc.rit.edu> writes:

:1) Is there any VAXstation hardware FAQ's out there? I looked hard, but
:came up with nothing.

  See the OpenVMS FAQ for pointers to available information sources.

:2) What kind of memory does it take. It looks like a 72-pin slot. Will
:parity or non parity, standard simms work, or are they DEC specific. Do
:they have to go in pairs, or what?

  The SIMMs are standard parity SIMMs, but if you choose non-Digital SIMMs,
  you should expect to have to perform, or to have some other organization
  perform, the necessary `integration and testing' work involved.  (I've
  seen good SIMMs, and I've seen flakey SIMMs, and I've seen SIMMs that
  don't meet the vendor's own timing ratings.)

:3) will any scsi hard drive work?

  Any?  None of the `S's in SCSI are `Standard'.  See previous answer.

:4) With SUN Sparc stations, if you have no keyboard, all communication
:will be routed through the serial port, is this the same with the vax
:station?

  The VAXstation can direct console I/O via a serial port, or via
  the workstation display.  By default, it goes to the workstation
  display.  If output does not appear on the console serial port
  during power-up, press <BREAK> a few times on the console terminal.

  The next question you may be asking may involve the MMJ (modified
  modular jack) pinout and connectors.  See the FAQ for the pinout.

:5) does a rom monitor exist, like on a sun, the machine goes to it for
:boot instructions and stuff? If so, how would I get the commands?

  The HELP command at the console `chevrons' prompt will provide you
  with an overview of the available commands.

  >>> HELP

