In article <526nta$hgq@newsbf02.news.aol.com>, jef451@aol.com (JEF451) writes:
|>Help - I have a DecPC466D2LP with 4x4 Meg memory and wish to increase
|>to larger memory. I understand the machine takes 16 meg simms but when I
|>install 1x16 Meg (60 ns, non-parity) - it isnt recognised. Ideally I would
|>like to mix this simm with 1 or more 4 meg simms or 8 meg simms.

There are "double-bank" SIMMs out there which are not recognized by older
machines like yours.  You need a SIMM which appears on the bus as a single
16M SIMM.  According to an excerpt of a spec, below, 8M SIMMs aren't supported.
Also, you can't mix sizes in a pair of banks (0/1, 2/3), and you can't have
"holes".  You would need two 16MB SIMMs in banks 0 and 1 before you could
use the 4MB SIMMs in banks 2 or 2/3.

     Upgrade support up to 64 MB of memory is provided through four 36-bit
     SIMM socket. Paged mode accesses are provided for maximum performance 
     utilized with every even bank pair of memory of the same DRAM size.
     
     Memory configruation

     The main logic board shall contain four simm sockets (sockets 
     designated as bank 0, 1, 2, 3) to support system memory 
     configuration up to 64MB using 4MB,16MB (70 ns) SIMMs. Each SIMM is
     36-bits wide, 72pins.
	
	---------------------------------------------
	| BANK0 | BANK1 | BANK2 | BANK3 | MEMORY MB |
	---------------------------------------------              
	| 1M    |       |       |       |       4   | 
	---------------------------------------------              
	| 1M    | 1M    |       |       |       8   | 
	---------------------------------------------              
	| 1M    | 1M    | 1M    |       |      12   |
	---------------------------------------------              
	| 1M    | 1M    | 1M    | 1M    |      16   |     
	---------------------------------------------              
	| 1M    | 1M    | 4M    |       |      24   |      
	---------------------------------------------               
	| 1M    | 1M    | 4M    | 4M    |      40   |                        
	---------------------------------------------              
	| 4M    |       |       |       |      16   |   
	---------------------------------------------              
	| 4M    | 4M    |       |       |      32   | 
	---------------------------------------------              
	| 4M    | 4M    | 4M    |       |      48   | 
	---------------------------------------------               
	| 4M    | 4M    | 4M    | 4M    |      64   |               
	---------------------------------------------

["1M" means a 1Mx36 4MB SIMM, "4M" meabs 4Mx36 16MB SIMM]
