In article <R.32446CC1.5526@norfolk.infi.net>, "Donald H. Griffin Jr." 
<dhgjr@norfolk.infi.net> writes:

|>I recently decided to upgrade from the standard 750 megabyte hard drive
|>and added another hard drive to my system.  I want to be able to have
|>both drives hooked up at the same time but I am only able to hook up one
|>or the other due to lack of connections on the cables.  I have been told
|>that I have to add a controller card ?  Does this make sense ?

Yes.  Your system has only a single channel IDE controller which means that
it can control at most two devices (hard disk and CD-ROM).  Later Starion
models have dual-channel EIDE controllers for four devices.  Add-on EIDE
controllers are cheap (under $50).
