Hey Dave,

I don't know if this will point you in the right path but after
numerous installs of DEC's (mylex's) SWXCR controller on Alpha
platforms (1000, 2000, 2100), I've had various "weird" problems
that DEC support was worthless on.  It essentially turned into 
replacing controller after controller till we found one that worked.

Recently I discovered that there is a problem with the SWXCR on Alpha 
when you run more than 8MB of SWXCR cache that results usually in 
hanging the system on boot up but also contributes to other strange 
problems.  If you have more than 8MB cache you will need to make sure 
that your firmware is of the latest version and you can download it from 
DEC's web page.  It has fairly vague instructions on how to install the 
firmware.

Hope this helps ?

