DEC might get annoyed, but legally I don't think that they could do
much about it.  It's like that chap who wrote a book which was
basically a step by step guide to being a "hit man".  Attempts were
made to prosecute him for writing a book explaining how to murder
people, holding him responsible for murders.  However, it was ruled
that he committed no crime.  If one can't be held liable for
publishing information about how to kill people, how can one be
considered to be a criminal for telling people how to rearrange some
magnetic bits on a spinning platter? :-)

