DEC license, and has no contractual agreements with DEC in any way,
whatsoever, figures out how to do something intersting with VMS and
wants to share this information with others, for purely, shall we say,
educational purposes, not to harm DEC, then this person has done no
harm.  However, if an unscrupulous business decides to use this
information to rearrange some bits on the spinning platters of a disk
attached to their VAX-9000 in order to be able to support a hundred
more users, then that business is the criminal, not the person who
posted the information.  It's that simple.  Some people may not like
it, and DEC may not like it, but that's just too bad.

