In article <323D83E6.4DF06909@triton.com>, Jay Olson wrote:
>I would like to add a second ethernet to my UDB/Multia. This variant has
>a single PCI slot which contains a small SCSI controller. The SCSI
>controller hooks up to an internal 3.5 inch disk and to an external SCSI
>connector.  
>
>Is there some sort of disk controller on the motherboard? I see a small
>connector with two rows of pins under the floppy which might be one. Is
>this a SCSI interface or an IDE interface or something else?

It should be an IDE interface.

It has been recommended to me that I not try to put a second disk drive in
there; the power supply is designed to handle the hardware that's in there,
with only enough to spare to handle the potential PCI card.

If you add an IDE drive, you should move the SCSI disk out, perhaps to an
external chassis.  I run a SCSI II cable out to a 5.25" SCSI drive that's
located and powered in my other PC's tower case.

>Assuming there is some sort of disk interface on the motherboard, are
>there any PCI ethernet cards which are small enough to fit in the case?

Apparently one can fit 100BaseT PCI Ethernet cards in there.
