Beta Testers wanted for Digigami MovieScreamer, the
'Fast-Start' QuickTime(tm) movie creation tool
---------------------------------------------------

Digigami, Inc. is looking for beta testers for MovieScreamer,
our multi-platform publishing and conversion 
tool for 'Fast-Start' QuickTime(tm) movies.

'Fast-Start' movies allow clients to play QuickTime movies 
before the entire movie has downloaded (i.e. streaming playback).
Such playback can be done via Digigami's CineWeb plug-ins for 
Netscape Navigator, through Navigator 3.0's built-in QuickTime 
plug-ins or anyone's elses QuickTime plug-in that is enabled for 
streaming playback.  Every QuickTime movie that will be 
downloaded via the Internet should be converted to the 
'Fast-Start' format.

'Fast-Start' QuickTime movies are standard 'flattened' movie 
files that have been 're-organized' for playback over the 
Internet (or corporate Intranets).  Note that they are a 
non-proprietary format, and played back in any standard 
QuickTime viewer just like regular QuickTime movies.


We are searching for beta testers who fall primarily into 
 three groups:

1. Unix Webmasters who have large amounts of existing 
QuickTime movies and want the ability to convert existing 
and/or new movies to the 'Fast-Start' format directly 
on their Unix web servers.
	
We are currently testing on the following platforms:

OS		Version		CPU
------------------------------------------
SunOS       4.1.x          SPARC
Solaris     2.x            SPARC
BSDI        2.x            Intel
SGI         5.2+           MIPS
DEC Ultrix  V4.3
DEC OSF/1   V3.2
HP HP/UX   (9000)
Linux       1.2            Intel

Ports to other Unix platforms are possible.  Please send specific
requests regarding ports to other platforms.

2. Windows NT Webmasters who have large amounts of existing 
QuickTime movies and want the ability to convert existing 
and/or new movies to the 'Fast-Start' format directly on 
their NT web servers.

Currently, MovieScreamer is availible for the Intel version of NT. 
We are currently considering ports to the other NT platforms 
(ALPHA, MIPS and/or the Power PC platform). Please send specific 
requests regarding ports to other platforms.


3. Persons using Netscape Navigator Gold who would like to beta 
test the Digigami MovieScreamer plug-in to convert existing 
QuickTime movies into 'Fast-Start' versions for placement on their 
Web pages. We are currently testing this plug-in on all Microsoft 
Windows platforms, including Windows 3.1, 95, and NT, with both 
16- and 32-bit versions of Netscape Navigator Gold 2.0 and 3.0.

