There is no difference between ANSI C on these platforms.
The problem is that people rarely adhere to ANSI C in a
meaningful way.

Anyhow things to watch out for:

Pointers are 64 bits on the Alpha and by default on UNIX
they put stuff in the high 32 bits, so be careful with
pointer kludges.

Longs are 64 bits, ints are 32.

There are no "near" and "far" specifiers on the DEC.

C really doesn't include much library definition.  This
is handled by other standards.  Things that DOS just took
from the UNIX implementations, probably will work, others
may be completely different.

-Ron



