Hi,

I wrote this piece of program:

static double FillBinomTable(double tab[], int b)
{
    double factor = 1.0 / pow(2.0, b);
    int n = b, m = 1;
    int i = 0;

    while (n != -1)
    {
        tab[i++] = factor;
        factor *= (double) n-- / (double) m++;
    }
}

which fills a table with binomial probabilities. The problem is that
when I use DEC's c compiler (with -g), 'factor' becomes 0.707106...,
which is sqrt(2), whereas when I use gcc, it becomes 1/(2**b). The
last one is correct.

Is this some kind of optimizer bug?

