I suppose it depends on what you mean by "saturate".

DEC and SGI can also saturate the bus, if by that you mean that
adding threads results in not increase in aggregate traffic.

I suspect that what you mean is that they achieve a larger fraction
of peak bandwidth.  To compare these, we need to include write-allocate
traffic (that I do not normally give credit for), which gives:

    machine	cpus	STREAM  w/allocates  	Peak	%
    -------------------------------------------------------
    SunUE6000	16	 1945	   2593		2500   104%
    SGI PwChl    8        750      1000         1200    83%
    DEC 8400/350 8       1132      1510          ???    ??%
    DEC 8400/300 8        978      1304         1600    82%
    -------------------------------------------------------

From these results, it appears that the Sun folks are getting
cache re-use, in violation of the intent of the benchmark....
This is also possibly effecting DEC and SGI results for eight
or more processors as well, though clearly not by too much.

Hmmm.....

I don't want to do this, but I may have to up the "base" config
to more than 16 MB/array, and then allow smaller configurations
by request....
