I'll throw-in my 64-bits worth of opinion:
Making a decision on what-platform-to-run-my-business-on isn't going
to be swayed by a one-time special deal nor a discount proffered to me
for being featured in an advertisement.  My business is more important
than that; and there's no shortage of studies that show that the
initial hardware acquisition cost is not where most of the money
eventually gets spent --- support, maintenance, training, etc. can be
bigger monetary factors.

Did Oracle get a price break for choosing Digital?  And did they get
some form of additional compensation for that advertisement? 
Probably.  But is it that hard of a stretch of the imagination to
think that Sun and HP and who-knows-who-else didn't approach Oracle
with similar offers?

