> I have VAXstation 3100 (KA42 cpu) with an RZ22 internal, and several older
> Seagate scsi disks on the external scsi bus.
> 
> I want to put a used Seagate ST3550N on the internal bus to replace the RZ22.
> The st3550 works perfectly on a pc (create partitiontables, file system,
> copying and reading files). The VAXstation reports device DKA300 (for scsi
> id3), and that it is a 426 MB st3550n which is as expected. The drive is
> jumpered to be always spun up.  I can do a low level format with test  76
> with no errors.
> 
> But when I try to access the drive eg $ init dka300: I get a fatal drive
> error, whether the drive is on the internal or external bus.
> 
> Anyone have any suggestions ?

I am not specifically familiar with the ST3550N, but many newer Seagate
drives require SCSI driver patches if you are running a version of VMS
prior to 6.2.  I think VAXSCSI03_061 is the current patch (it applies to
VMS 5.5-2 as well).

Good luck!

