Hi fellow home VAX owner!
First, NETBsd will not work (not ported ) to any of these boxes..only microvax 
2 and 750,were ported as of 4 months ago..Anyone can correct me on this, as I 
gave up trying to get this to work on a Microvax 2. (couldn't get the part 
table right for my ESDI drives).

Now the good news...try this first, to get into VMS.

Turn on computer, use the halt button on the back to stop the machine when it 
starts the boot program (after test 1..)
you will get >>> prompt
type B/1
and hit returm.
You should get ,
SYSBOOT>  prompt type SET UAF 1
SYSBOOT > then type CONT
you could also enter SET START "MIN" at the SYSBOOT> prompt to bypass al the 
meaty stuff that makes the startup slow.
The system should come up ok....now try logging in. username: SYSTEM
you should get 2 password prompts, just type return key.
You should get a DCL $ prompt or whatever the pref. owner set it too.
now rename the [sysexe]sysuaf.dat file the something else,shutdown the system 
and reboot B/1
SET UAF 0
SET START ""
CONT
this time, you still login the same way...now rename [sysexe]sysuaf.dat back 
to this name.
set def [sysexe]
run authorize
mod system/pass=123456   This sets the sysstem password to 123456
exit
You can now  login with your new system password and run normally agian..

If you have problems, email me at dlm@io.org

Good luck!         -Doug-



