Here's what the LA210 letter printer user's guide has to say about
this:

Note: The switch on the left is A, the on on the right is B.

A1 - Speed control/restraint protocol switch.  Down (factory setting)
     for transmission restraint using the EIA BUSY control line.  Up 
     for speed control using the EIA SPDI (sped indicator) and SPDS 
     (speed select) control lines.  

A2 - Modem control switch for access to modem control.  Down (factory
     setting) for no modem control.  Up for modem control.

A3 & A4 - Fault response switches - select the response to a paper 
     fault when it occurs.

     Function                Switch settings
                                 3       4
   select no action             down    down (factor setting)
  (XOFF is sent if enabled)
   select to send break signal   up     down    
   select disconnect (drop DTR) down     up
   select do not connect         up      up

A5 - end of transmission switch - controlls the EOT (end of transmission)
     characters.  Down (factory setting) disables coded disconnect 
     (ignore EOT).  Up to enable coded disconnect (disconnect upon
     receiving EOT).

A6 - XON/XOFF protocol switch.  Up (factory setting) enables auto 
     XON/XOFF.  Down disables XON/XOFF.

A7 - Error procesing switch, controls receiver error processing.
     Down (factory setting) to set receiver processing to print
     substitute character.  Up sets receiver error processing to
     print characters as received.

A8 - Store features switch - stores the computer selectable features in 
     user permanent memory.  These features are as follows:

     horizontal tab     paper width
     vertical tab       answerback message   
     form length        character set selection and mapping
     horizontal pitch   pitch mode 
     vertical pitch     end of line control
     horizontal margins new line request
     vertical margins   C1 receive
     paper alignment    C2 receive

     To verify that these features are stored:
     1. set the printer ff-line
     2. turn the power on and off
     3. print the status message.

     To store or change these features, reset the desired configuration
     switches and then move switch A8 from down to up.  When moving A8 
     from up to down: nothing happens.  The factory defaults for some
     features are listed in the status message.  The default settings
     which aren't listed are:

     feature              setting

     left margin          column 1
     right margin         paper width=132 columns
     top margin           line 1
     bottom margin        form length=66 lines
     paper alignment      offset=0
     paper width          13.2 inches   
  

B1 through B5 - baud rate select.

   BPS           Switch settings
                   1  2  3  4  5       

   50              d  d  d  d  d
   75              u  d  d  d  d
   110             d  u  d  d  d
   134.5           u  u  d  d  d
   150             d  d  u  d  d
   200             u  d  u  d  d
   300             d  u  u  d  d
   600             u  u  u  d  d
   1200            d  d  d  u  d
   1800            u  d  d  u  d
   2400            d  u  d  u  d
   4800(fctry set) u  u  d  u  d
   7200            d  d  u  u  d
   9600            u  d  u  u  d

   75/600          d  d  d  d  u
   75/1200         u  d  d  d  u
   150/600         d  u  d  d  u
   150/1200        u  u  d  d  u
   300/2400        d  d  u  d  u
   300/4800        u  d  u  d  u
   600/2400        d  u  u  d  u
   600/4800        u  u  u  d  u


B6 & B7 - data parity switches

    Parity     Switch settings
  7-bit  8-bit    6  7

  space  none     d  d (factory setting)
  mark   none     u  d
  even   even     d  u
  odd    odd      u  u

B8 - data format switch - the printer may send and receive data in 
     either 7-bit or 8-bit ASCII mode for character processing.
     Up (factory setting) for eight data bits, down for seven.


The switches also have some other functions when used with the
plug-in interface adapter.

