Copyright is not the only issue.  You see - you *don't* own the software.
DEC does not *sell* anybody VMS, they *license* it out.  This is much more
like renting a video than it is buying a book.  When you rent a video you
do not own it, when you license software you do not own it.  You own the
right to use it for as long as the license is valid. Now, it is true that
most licenses you get from DEC are permanant - they let you run the version
