nbz32017@pegasus.cc.ucf.edu (Nikolay B Zeldovich) writes:

> 
> sorry if i'm somehow out of track, but how come noone is discussing Cray
> machines? are they already slower than Ultras+Alphas, way ahead, or their
> OS isn't good (which i heard from some people)?

The biggest of the current Cary line is the T3E which turns out to be
a massively parallel array of Alphas. It is an awesome computing
engine as are most of its brethren like the YMP C90 and the newer
J90. But these are poor transaction machines as they are simply not
designed to have the I/O bandwidth needed for transaction
processing. They are pure number crunching machines and to achieve
this, other aspects of performance were sacrificed.

The C90 might be able to turn a fair TPC number, as it does have
reasonable I/O performance, but the machine is simply not designed for
this and the cost of using the system for this would be
astronomical. (If Cray is still building the C90.)

