I suspect that not too many people are interested in TPC-D results for the
more "traditional" Cray machines (PVP and MPP), since they aren't used for
commercial databases; but if you are referring to the former division of
Cray (Business Systems) which produced the 64 processor Sparc-based
"superservers," it is now owned by Sun Microsystems. 

