I need some suggestions.  Last night my dUnix 4.0 system stopped
letting people login.  It would accept the username and password, and
display the message about last successful and unsuccessful logins (I
have enhanced security in place) and then hang.  This even happened
from the console.

I did notice that repeated attempts caused no change in the
success/unsuccess report so that probably limits how far into the
login process it got.  

Nothing in syslog or console messages indicate anything. In fact they
tend to be very light on any messages of any kind, but that may just
indicate a drop is usage.

Authck reported that everything was fine, including the terminal data
base, which I've seen cause problems like this in the past.

It didn't appear to affect anybody already on the system.

Nothing unusually appears to have been happening on the system
according to ps.

Rebooting the system caused the problem to go away.

Now my users are reporting that they've been seeing the same behavior
in the past on a transient basis -  they just never bothered to tell
me.  I've also had a couple of reports that logins where rejected with
the message,

telnetd: All network ports in use.

which I find very hard to believe.

Anybody have any ideas of what's going on, or even what I should look
at next time this happens?  I've been thinking in terms of a lock not
being released somewhere, but I'm guessing.
 
