A friend of mine (who does not have access to newsgroups) ran into the
following problem: he needs to attach a 5.25'' floppy drive to an
AlphaServer 400 running OpenVMS. The Alpha has FD controller on an ISA
slot. ISA devices are not 
capable of being probed for configuration information by OpenVMS. A user
must enter
 ISA  information manually using the ISA configuration utility (ISACFG).
This utility is a part of SRM console. ISACFG allows to modify an entry
in config database for adding new device. Database has entry for a 3.5"
drive but not for a 5.25" drive. If anybody knows how to configure a
5.25" drive with ISACFG, please respond to 

