In article <50qpf8$fgr@nn1.fast.net>, kshuff@fast.net (kshuff) writes:

>  After installing a TZ30 tape drive into a DecStation 3100 running Ultrix 
>4.2, my question is how do you get Ultrix to recognize it. I successfully ran 
>"MAKEDEV tz0" and it installed all the appropriate device names. Do I have to 
>do a new configuration, or rebuild the kernal?

If the SCSI ID of the tape was 0 then you should be done.  Left to
itself, the procedure that builds the configuration file for ULTRIX
will always add all device entries for any particular SCSI controller,
so there shouldn't be anything there to do.  On the other hand, if
the tape drive isn't SCSI ID 0, then you created device for the wrong
device.  Since the DECstation 3100 only has a single SCSI bus, the
device name is tz{SCSI-ID}.

>-Keith S. Huff
>
