I agree.  I've seen too many hardware shipping dates slip, 
and, software shipping dates turn out to be extended beta
tests with sympathetic customers.  By availability, I mean,
when does Josephina User get her hardware/software?  But, 
I concede that there is a point to the following:


|> 	I tend to disagree somewhat, I believe because of the
|> 	money involved with large system purchases you have to plan
|> 	for quite a while.  A 6 month or so wait for availability

Especially, with product cycles so short now, customers need
more information up front.  Products don't just sit there in
production for 3 years, like they used to.  The problem is,
though, how do we keep the playing field level for the honest
producers?


|> 	isn't so bad.  However, I do feel there should be
