Tania Bedrax-Weiss <tania@cirl.uoregon.edu> writes:

> I'm really tempted to buy an Alpha 21066-166Mhz but don't have any idea
> of how they perform (compared to an Intel) or if they had had any
> hardware problems.  Anyone with experience in this system?

If you're referring to a UDB (aka Multia) then the consensus seems to
be that you can expect P75-P90-like performance.  Obviously, your
mileage varies greatly depending on what you're doing.  The UDB is
quite a bit slower than other Alphas that run at similar clock speeds.
The reason for this is that the memory system of that machine is
underpowered.  But considering that the price of the entire box
($550-800) is less than what the graphics card alone normally goes
for, it's quite a deal.

Judging based on the traffic, tons of people have recently bought such
boxes to run Linux.  You might want to tune into axp-list@redhat.com
for more info/experiences (the list is archived at www.redhat.com).

