>vendor thinks that PM consists of cleaning the terminal screens
>and no more.   The system in question is a pair of MicroVAXes
>in BA123 boxes.

Cleaning terminal screens as preventive maint.???  What about the
inside of the terminals?  It gets quite dusty inside of terminals and
they need to be cleaned out inside from time to time.  Perhaps the
best way to protect your equipment is to take the heaviest piece that
you have and hit your repairman over the head with it, so as to
protect your equipment from future service calls. :-) I wouldn't want
a repairman who considers preventive maint. to consist of just screen
cleaning anywhere near my equipment.

>Are there any generally-accepted standards for Preventative
>Maintenance?   What does your service provider do for PM?
>What do you think they should do?   How often?

I don't know about what any repairmen do; I just know what I do for my
own equipment.

