PG> sell what it has benchmarked at most 6 months after the benchmark
PG> results are made public. What this means is that the DBMS and
PG> systems companies have entered a mode where new machines/releases
PG> are benchmarked way before the actual hardware/software can be
PG> bought. If the hw/sw being benchmarked is not available 6 months
PG> after the benchmark date, the benchmark must be withdrawn. Big 
