the TD1 (plug for XKL).  I like the concept of a super computer that 
is a gofaster machine built on MIPS or other risc chips.  

If I could, I would keep both Cray Research and Cray Computer around
to inspire other go faster efforts.  Reality sets in however and we
can't always get what we want.

I do have hopes that the name Cray will stay around.
WHether it is on a box that runs alphas or mips or motos or hp doesn't
really matter as much as the power of the box, the capability to run the
problem and not having a kludged up system.

