Howard Joffe wrote:
> 
> We have an ALPHA 3000 running Open VMS AXP 6.1.  We are thinking of
> switching the operating system to Windows NT. What effect would this have
> on files and executables created under VMS?  Are there any other pitfalls
> to doing this? Such as things not supported under NT, that work under
> VMS.

Firstly, Windows NT won't run on any of the 3000 series Alphas: there's no 
support for TurboChannel.

Assuming you did have an Alpha that could run OpenVMS and Windows NT, 
installing a different operating system on a different disk wouldn't affect the 
OpenVMS files and executables at all, it's just that you couldn't read them 
(Windows NT doesn't understand File-11/ODS-2), and if you could, you couldn't 
run the binaries (it's a different operating system), and you might not be 
able to read the files (Windows NT doesn't understand RMS).
-- 
