from the network. I break out into the console and looked at the
configuration
of slot 3 (the standard system slot). All three disk drives are shown at
SCSI ids 2 3 and 0 (the original drive). 2 & 3 are the RZ23's borrowed
from another DEC) 0 is a RZ23L which I think is slightly bigger.

The problem is this: in the DEC manual for the 5000/240 it says to boot
from a disk drive to use boot 3/rz0/vmunix (or similar, where rzX
corresponds to the SCSI ID). My DEC is  5000/150. When I try this on
disks 0 and 3 the drives spin up the first time, churn a while and the
break out with

KN04 2.1K (PC=xxxxxxxx SP=xxxxxxxxx)

which i presume is the program counter and stack pointer.

