Don't know for sure.  But I'd *assume* the answer is yes, unless
you've had it under a maintenance contract.  I see that with the new
HSx50 controllers, Digital is separating the hardware from the
firmware; dunno if that goes for older stuff too or not.

> Is v8.6 the highest upgrade? Any known problems?

Stay away from V8.5.  I hear that V8.6 corrects the cache problem with
V8.5. . .V8.5 was the first version to support the entire 64Mb cache
that was in some controllers (such as the HSC95) instead of just 32Mb. 
And that had some problems under some circumstances --- hit some
sites, but not others; apparently very load-dependent.  (We saw the
problem the day after we upgraded --- reading some files gave us the
wrong data!  We backed-down to V8.3 (never installed V8.4) that
night.)  Now that V8.6 is out, we no longer have HSC's with 64Mb
cache; so we're in no hurry to upgrade now.

Scott
