In article <1996Aug30.122330@stsci.edu>, speck@stsci.edu writes:
|>I'm trying to replace an old macro USEROPEN routine with a Fortran routine.
|>
|>And here is the Fortran (without comments) with which I'm trying to replace it:

..
|>	    ! set the UFO and CBT bits 
|>	    fab.fab$l_fop = fab$v_ufo .OR. fab$v_cbt

Should be:
	    fab.fab$l_fop = fab.fab$l_fop .OR. fab$m_ufo .OR. fab$m_cbt
|>
|>            ! set the UPI bit
|>            fab.fab$b_shr = fab$v_upi

Should be:
	    fab.fab$b_shr = fab.fab$b_shr .OR. fab$m_upi

|>
|>	    ! open the file, return on error
|>	    open_old_chan = sys$open(fab)
|>
|>	    if (open_old_chan .eq. 0) then

Should be:
	    if (.not. open_old_chan) then

Try these corrections and see if things improve.  The fab$v_ symbols are
bit offset numbers, not masks.  Alternatively, you could use the IBSET
intrinsic.
