I I'm not aware of any support by Vaxen or Alphas either, and even if the CPU
hardware would support it, there is nothing in VMS like doing a "warm start"
after a battery backed-up break (as far I know at least).

However, the best direction to look for is into UPS (Uninterruptible (?) Power
Supplies), the way the more expensive Alpha-servers are surviving power breaks.
There are even manufacturers of UPS systems, which support VMS software (and not
only Unix or PC systems as most UPS), i.e. software which do a controlled VMS
shutdown in case the break exceeds the battery capacity.
I don't have the companies names at hand, if You don't find some in USA, have a
look into www.transtec.de, they are selling these things in Europe.
