The installation manual (or user guide) lists the various codes and gives you
the commonest reason for each of them. Unfortuanetly some time between installing
my KDA50s and now I have mislaid that manual :-(.

However, I do remember that the commonest reason for a problem is that there
is a break in grant continuity - so make sure that there are no empty slots.
(If this is a VAXstation 3200 in a BA23 - which is how I think they shipped -
don't forget that the signals follow a serpentine pattern after the first 3
rows. The easiest way to configure is to make sure that all slots after the
first 3 rows are filled with something.

|>I may have made an installation mistake when I installed the boards, all 
|>I did was set the address on the boards and install them.
