Dan Tso (Dantso@cris.com) wrote:
: 	The problem is that the Ultrix DHU-11/DHV-11 driver for some reason
: does not support 38400 because that speed code was omitted from the internal
: driver table. Why one can only speculate. 


That driver has been around for a long time, from early 4BSD
distributions (some of it is no doubt derived from UNIX version 6 or 7
code for the DHU-11).

As for why the 38400 speed code was omitted, the answer is fairly simple.  
While the DHU-11 can drive the line at 38400, many vaxen (like my uVax 
II/GPX, for example) can't keep up with the interrupts to receive data at 
that rate, and drop characters as a result.  The code was never modified 
when faster vaxen came along...

