>>>>> "LDB" == Larry D Bohan, <lbohan@dbc.com> writes:
In article <32276909.100305651@news.ccnet.com> lbohan@dbc.com (Larry D Bohan, Jr) writes:
LDB> for what purposes do you all use a memory channel 
LDB> interconnect betw your workstations?  
--

Primarily parallel computing using something like "PVM".

I've had a MemoryChannel (beta) for about a year - it's very low
latency (~15 microseconds using PVM, ~4 using native API) network
with reasonable bandwidth.

There are other options - Myrinet (higher latency, but better
bandwidth and it's switched, but a hub). Fast Ethernet (cheap as all
get out, and reasonable bandwidth, but sucky latency).

However, MemoryChannel holds a lot of promise as a direct-memory
network, and a lot of people want the low-latency it offers.



