Well.........

First up the Sun won't run Solaris 2. The last version of SunOs it can
run I think is 4.1.1. Second, depending on the age of the machine you
may not be able to load the OS from CD, (depends on versions of
boot PROM). So to update the SunOS you'd need to find a 1/4" tape.....

The good news is that your machine may be upgradable to a SPARC based
system (the first SPARC's were Sun 3's with a SPARC VME processor
card). If you can find a source (look in the SUN newsgroups) this
would allow you to run Solaris and give a performance boost.

You can also run NetBSD on the Sun (supports Sun3 and SPARC) I believe
this is faster than Solaris.

With the VaxStation you are stuck with finding a version of Ultrix,
there is no free Unix for this machine.

Bottom line here is this.

 If you can afford it buy a PC and run Linux or BSD. The bang for buck
is the best you can get. If you have only a little money, download
NetBSD for the Sun3 and actively research if you can upgrade the
Processor Card to SPARC.

 Retire the VAX they are of about equal power but the Sun can be
upgraded and has a Free Unix.

Quin





